      "id": "50098245",
      "title": "Show HN: TowerPanic – a family party game on a small FastAPI realtime engine",
      "url": "https://towerpanic.com/",
      "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50098245",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "points": 2,
      "comments": 2,
      "author": "ms209495",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-15T02:02:26Z",
      "storyText": "I want to show you the game I created recently and tell you whole the story&#x2F;experience - including backend&#x2F;latency&#x2F;scalability.<p>You can try it quickly without an account - I created game demo rooms (EU&#x2F;US&#x2F;JP) - links below - just be aware that anyone with a link can access join the game.<p>Let&#x27;s start with short description of the game itself:<p>This is the TowerPanic game - you are standing on one of four towers, during each round some of towers crack, and some of these lean, and finally one of these colapse - you need to watch out to not be on the failing one.\nIt&#x27;s a multiplayer game for whole family.\nThis can be also used as an icebreaking game - for people in any age.\nThe game is safe for children - no violence, no strangers, no chat, no ads.\nParent creates an account (free 14-day trial, then a paid pass) and starts the game - others join using a QR code or a link.<p>Behind the game there is an interesting backend engine - I willdescribe it in a moment.<p>Let&#x27;s start with the history of this whole project:\n- I was playing with asyncio and fastapi\n- As an exercise I created a reliable chat application (multiple rooms, in each room each user can reliably broadcast a message to all other users)\n- I extracted communication to separate layer - creating network&#x2F;application layer interfaces - &#x27;reliable client&#x27; interface for client and &#x27;state machine&#x27; interface for the service on server.\n- With these interfaces - I was able to create other service - an &#x27;sgame&#x27; (simple game). With verified interfaces and created services (chat, sgame) I was able to ask AI to generate other tools&#x2F;games - I was impressed by these results\n- the games&#x2F;tools worked well - I deployed them on a remote server - I was surprised that the latency was very good - almost everything worked smoothly<p>I tested the tools and games with my children and one of the game was really great.\nI decided to make this game public - I chose &#x27;TowerPanic&#x27; name for it.<p>I prepared an account&#x2F;payment server for this game (as a separate FastAPI application).\nThis was very good choice:\n- the game servers keep rooms only in memory - nothing persistent (rooms have expiration date)\n- the account server keeps all persistent data (it uses database)<p>Because of this split I was able to figure out how to upgrade and scale frontend and backend independently - without significantly impacting users.<p>I optimized the communication layer - so that it works in finite memory - only finite number of recent messages is kept, and I sent a full service snapshot (full state) to the lagging clients.<p>The backend process (FastAPI&#x2F;python) is limited by python GIL (only one core can be utilized) - to utilize all server cores I used HAProxy with consistent hashing to distribute rooms - so that users can be redirected to proper backend process.<p>I tested how many rooms a single server can handle - it handles hundreds of active rooms in parallel with no significant latency drop.<p>Before making it public I noticed that latency in other region of world might be higher and this could influence UX - I confirmed this using artificial delay on my remote server.<p>I decided to deploy the application in three regions - EU, US, JP - to ensure low latency (below 150ms) in most of the world.\nThe room is created in region closest to the user (best latency from the browser to backend).<p>I needed also to prepare some legal documents (terms, privacy, refunds) - thanks to AI this was much easier.\nI&#x27;m a backend engineer, frontend&#x2F;UI&#x2F;UX were designed by me but code was generated by AI.<p>To summerize all this work:\n- I&#x27;m happy that I was able to deliver complete game&#x2F;complete product\n- I think the whole work took me about 20 evenings - I&#x27;m impressed that it was so short - I think this is because the technology I used is popular and all fits well \n- AI was great as a peer (to discuss the options for distributing the load, discuss were to locate servers, or discuss how auth&#x2F;payments work under the hood, ... - based on this I could choose the best option)\n- AI was great for doing the non work which I&#x27;m doing ineffectively (frontend&#x2F;UI&#x2F;legal docs).<p>The game is available at <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;towerpanic.com&#x2F;?ref=hn\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;towerpanic.com&#x2F;?ref=hn</a><p>I will appreciate your comments&#x2F;feedback:<p>Product:\n - did you meet any obstacles to play ?\n - how smoothly it worked ? - please specify your location if it didn&#x27;t work well \n - most important thing&#x2F;things to improve ?\n - anything else ...\nSolution&#x2F;Engineering:\n - one thing you will change in the architecture &#x2F; approach ?\n - anything else ...<p>If you don&#x27;t want to register you can play directly using below links (2 rooms for each location, max 10 players in each room&#x2F;board). Choose best location:<p>DEMO ROOMS (expire: 19 October 2026 at 22:00 UTC):<p>EU:\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-de-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn1&#x2F;join&#x2F;AUB3lS3Y_OgNjOTgIPW-gmT9eL2OENrGKL-EnTRj43dk5YoqEm7nSvu4NsIoRv4vrn0arNX0Jfcqi5SBDCf1grr-2e38H5CwGx9PZKWv1AjTFsmH_FbyguZyelTGEPdx1j36OCKm1Hw\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-de-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn1&#x2F;join&#x2F;AUB3lS3Y_...</a>\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-de-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn4&#x2F;join&#x2F;ASlA3J43Ucjbg0NG3r3AcDjAHiN22get0BmtWbQ-etLMYpLGVBCpUOHqirTJFTZhVo2mtCPj8cM5jNyoV5BQ_aO5HwoalFpiPPM9-yZ3t23HWP7lmwZ5EvXkDMgsk-khMF9TY2cQWb8\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-de-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn4&#x2F;join&#x2F;ASlA3J43U...</a><p>US:\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-us-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn2&#x2F;join&#x2F;AUCCS_x9dcXsGvvgRRLBfnOzqmPuZbZS5UWCh4InVBZ3X1PF985HDHe9EhQNO56mmcXcKlyE1jZD5CauwzweuEuCtMZu1_5Rba-XnCiVWICHsOfLHCIL-QUqV-uBQi2M5a03FaK_qD8\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-us-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn2&#x2F;join&#x2F;AUCCS_x9d...</a>\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-us-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn5&#x2F;join&#x2F;AVQbs_01N_sCaDumnrfsEdabzH1Ix4nW_TaLmfN-0FffOsKWBoEcugjtglTOnxg49psdPfA_a_D_FU1EB04q6Hu_qaG1HosdvAS_6586tVsdDIViXMA1tThzljpewJUJ6K2BtMiCEjk\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-us-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn5&#x2F;join&#x2F;AVQbs_01N...</a><p>JP:\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-jp-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn3&#x2F;join&#x2F;Afj600qp5jUrC7w2k0h2RuBRYJeqqOCigdw36VfvDBL_a0bCxsTMkot93jmcrkOBHqALZoN28PZZOzdHlv9hw6G7pjweEwGtmk1iVLxf9hNIXLsoPko2coUz5o2KFduQa4PnaqA5tGM\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-jp-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn3&#x2F;join&#x2F;Afj600qp5...</a>\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-jp-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn6&#x2F;join&#x2F;AUpDUuB1WsSq2GaNUHkRCDdqi1xYmzyKBGqmGpYg7CzsRjI4LyH8xsbWgSuOoE95kaGdRsyah-ImtmzKjkCaONXjNOfsihm9BuroOsLjfIHqPuOoMGtZ6X72qj4e7SRPvkyZuw1EF7o\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;engine.prod-jp-1.towerpanic.com&#x2F;b&#x2F;hn6&#x2F;join&#x2F;AUpDUuB1W...</a>",
